{"cluster_id": "C-3719", "topic": "`quiesce_cluster` falsely marked S08 inconclusive because it failed immediately ", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B021-027"], "canonical_claim": "`quiesce_cluster` falsely marked S08 inconclusive because it failed immediately on any transient non-empty `replication_queue.last_exception` instead of applying the sibling backlog-stall grace period; commit `35faaae182c` added the grace period and two regression tests.", "issue_ids": ["S08"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-19-campaign-38-results.md#L10-L12", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-19-campaign-38-results.md#L51-L69"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3720", "topic": "Consolidated Seven ASan gtest findings were test-lifetime bugs rather than pro", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-082", "B021-038"], "canonical_claim": "Seven ASan gtest findings were test-lifetime bugs rather than product bugs: six stack-use-after-scope cases came from an event-sink vector declared after `Pool`, and `CasPoolShutdown.UnresolvedWedgeSkipsFarewell` had a heap-use-after-free from reading `store->layout()` after `store.reset()`. Additionally, An ASan battery run found 7 genuine memory-safety bugs among 49 peeled aborts: 6 stack-use-after-scope instances in `CasSweepLateLog`-family tests, root-caused to an event-sink lambda capturing a local `events` vector declared AFTER the `Pool` object, so `~Pool` emits terminate events into the already-destroyed vector (fixed by declaring the vector before the Pool); and 1 heap-use-after-free in `CasPoolShutdown.UnresolvedWedgeSkipsFarewell`, root-caused to a `const Layout &` held across `store.reset()` (fixed by taking it by value).", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-19-session-full-summary.md#L45-L61", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-17-unattended-r5-r6-round.md#L57-L74"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3721", "topic": "Consolidated The CAS gtest battery's established `Cas*", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B021-040", "B027-111", "B034-111"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS gtest battery's established `Cas*:CA*:...` filter had never matched about 89\u201390 tests in the `CaWiring*`, `CaTransaction*`, `CaDedupCache*`, `CaInlinePlacement*`, and `CaPartPathParser*` suites; correcting the filter exposed three bugs in `gtest_ca_wiring.cpp`. Additionally, The obvious CAS gtest filter `Cas*:CA*` under-selects entire families such as `RefWriter*` and `CaWiring*`; the release gate must enumerate test families explicitly. Additionally, The CAS gate filter `Cas*:CA*` omitted `CaWiring`, `CaLifecycle`, several `RefWriter*` suites, and `RefTableCacheEviction`; twenty suites, including 17 CAS-relevant suites, were unclaimed by the gate.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/BACKLOG.md#gate-suite-list-omits-third-recurrence", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-19-session-full-summary.md#L81-L98", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-28-cas-merge-layout-preparation-design.md#verification"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3722", "topic": "Consolidated Constructing `ReadBufferFromMemoryFileBase` with `owns_memory=tru", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B024-030", "B024-031"], "canonical_claim": "Constructing `ReadBufferFromMemoryFileBase` with `owns_memory=true` and empty data can pass `nullptr` from `std::string_view::data()` to `memcpy` with length zero, violating the nonnull contract under UBSan. Additionally, The empty-file `ReadBufferFromMemoryFileBase` fix is to skip `memcpy` when `data.empty()`; no bytes need copying and the owned buffer must still construct at EOF.", "issue_ids": ["PR #2073", "STID 5930-5afa"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-22-pr2073-sanitizer-aborts.md#L253-L323"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3723", "topic": "The mount-lease renewal classifier, GCS conditional dialect tests, and dedup-log", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B024-032"], "canonical_claim": "The mount-lease renewal classifier, GCS conditional dialect tests, and dedup-log null-writer tests exposed `LOGICAL_ERROR` construction behavior that aborts debug or sanitizer builds before `catch` can run.", "issue_ids": ["PR #2073"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-22-pr2073-sanitizer-aborts.md#L1-L22"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3724", "topic": "The `DispatchThrowStillDrains` test was racy because it could cancel the first s", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B025-041"], "canonical_claim": "The `DispatchThrowStillDrains` test was racy because it could cancel the first scheduled task before task entry; a latch must prove that already-running work is drained before dispatch unwinds.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-24-codex-stage1-reviews.md#round-1"]}
