{"cluster_id": "C-3731", "topic": "Consolidated `CaRefWriterCleanupCore_empty_builds", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B030-108", "B030-109", "B030-121"], "canonical_claim": "`CaRefWriterCleanupCore_empty_builds.cfg` reported a temporal violation for `StalePrecommitEventuallyGone` even though `Builds = {}` makes `StaleExists` false and `NoStale` true in every behavior. Additionally, The empty-build temporal violation was a defect in supplied TLC 2.19 (2024-08-08, revision `5a47802`), not a model defect: the same jar falsely rejected the tautology `EventuallyTrue == <> TRUE`. Additionally, `CaRefWriterCleanupCore_empty_builds.cfg` violates the temporal property `StalePrecommitEventuallyGone` under TLC 2.19, although the same model's independent invariant `NoStale` passes on the four-state graph.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/2026-07-30-empty-set-survey.md#caref-writer-cleanup-core-false-temporal-violation", "docs/superpowers/models/2026-07-30-empty-set-survey.md#non-green-tlc-tails"]}
