{"cluster_id": "C-3745", "topic": "Consolidated `PutHookBackend", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B050-056", "B050-064", "B050-065"], "canonical_claim": "`PutHookBackend::casPut` previously bypassed its immediate parent `HidingListBackend::casPut`, silently disabling `before_cas_put` and `ambiguous_cas_count` fault injection when composed. Additionally, `PutHookBackend : HidingListBackend : CountingBackend`; therefore `PutHookBackend::casPut` must route through `HidingListBackend::casPut` to compose both hook layers.; `CasRefRecoveryCasWalk.PutHookBackendComposesHidingListBackendCasPutFaultInjection` arms both hook layers and verifies that both fire for one `casPut` call.", "issue_ids": ["T8"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/tidy-fix-draft-report.md#L42-L51", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/tidy-fix-report.md#L107-L113", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/tidy-fix-report.md#L91-L99"]}
